.TH AVR\-VM\-PAUSE 1 "" "avr 0.2.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-pause \- Pause a RUNNING Linux VM while preserving its disk.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm pause
[OPTIONS] VM_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pause a RUNNING Linux VM while preserving its disk.
.PP
By default the snapshot is disk-only: the filesystem survives, but resume performs a fresh boot and running processes do not. Pass --memory to also preserve guest memory and continue processes from where they stopped.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-memory\fR
Include guest memory and device state so running processes continue on resume.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the VM reaches PAUSED before returning.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
Seconds to wait when --wait is set. (default: 300)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the raw API response as JSON.
